# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the disaggregation step-1 window (docs/tp4-disagg-step1.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/disagg and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry. Templates only.
# D2: the TP2 PAIR (cards M and A) on the current image: the prefill and decode factors r and k of the disaggregation model, measured on the stock G1 path against D1's TP4 run of
# the SAME image, prompts and shapes. general-2link is the only pair profile that opens on this cabling (the p150_x2 profiles, c2-packed and c2-packed-prefix among them, declare
# four channels per edge and STRICT_INIT refuses M-A's two; the contract refuses the fast path, qwen_fast_t16, on the two-link pair), so this arm is G1 (no speculative decoding)
# at 4 seats x 65,536: no pair profile serves 8 seats, a 128k or 262k prompt, or the fast path on this cabling.
# NO RESET HERE: a pair-only reset leaves M's and A's links to B and C untrained; push it straight after X0 (a four-card reset). C2_CARDS is left unset (pair), as J2r/J3r.
# Shapes: prefill 1x4096, 1x32768, 1x60000 (the TTFT of a lone stream; 60k is the pair profile's top), decode 1/2/4 live at 4k and 4 live at 32k (steady rate per user).
# agreement: the TP2 greedy answers, for tp_agreement.py compare against D1's agreement-general-tp4-bench.json (the TP2-vs-TP4 exactness question).
# READ: bench-general-2link.json (per shape: max_ttft_s, median and steady tok/s per user), agreement-general-2link.json; the smoke log clean. Duration (estimate): 30-50 min
# (engine build 10-20 min, bench ~15 min, agreement 5-10 min; the pair smoke step's limit is 70 min).
C2_ACTIONS=smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_PROFILE=general-2link
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,bench,agreement
C2_BENCH_SHAPES=1x4096,1x32768,1x60000,2x4096,4x4096,4x32768
